        spokenEn: "Qutub Minar was commenced in 1199 by Qutb-ud-din Aibak to mark the founding of the Delhi Sultanate. Successor Shams-ud-din Iltutmish added three storeys, and after lightning struck in 1368, Firoz Shah Tughlaq restored the summit with white marble, creating a 72.5m brick minaret.",
