        spokenEn: "Towering 410 feet above Jodhpur on a perpendicular cliff, Mehrangarh was founded in 1459 by Rao Jodha of the Rathore dynasty. Described by Rudyard Kipling as \"the work of giants,\" its burnished red sandstone battlements enclose some of the most intricate royal courtyards in Rajasthan.",
