        spokenEn: "The Gateway of India was conceived to commemorate the historic landing of King George V and Queen Mary in Bombay in December 1911. Designed by architect George Wittet, the foundation stone was laid in 1913, and the grand triumphal arch was formally opened on December 4, 1924.",
