        spokenEn: "The Jagannath Temple of Puri is one of the four sacred Char Dham pilgrimage centers of Hinduism. Founded in the 12th century by Eastern Ganga King Anantavarman Chodaganga Deva, it enshrines wooden deities of Lord Jagannath, Balabhadra, and Subhadra, celebrated worldwide for the annual Ratha Yatra festival.",
