        spokenEn: "Anchoring a massive multi-palace complex atop a 150-foot fragile sedimentary cliff required multi-tiered stone retaining walls and gravity-draining terracotta conduits down to the Tawi bed. Subterranean stone vaults housed armories, artillery magazines, and royal treasuries connected by defended access routes.",
